C R161 OL DEP-003 | MUST | For every NuGet or npm addition or update, determine the latest stable version compatible with target framework/runtime and peers, verify it from the registry rather than memory, and never select preview/alpha/beta/RC/dev/nightly/prerelease or floating versions unless the user explicitly requested them ('latest' means latest stable compatible). | Dependency additions and updates | Explicit user request for prerelease/floating.
C R162 OL DEP-004 | MUST | Before installation, confirm the selected package/version is not deprecated, check known vulnerability information (dotnet package list --vulnerable --include-transitive, npm audit, advisories) with context and without upgrading or replacing unrelated packages because of a finding, and verify the exact version's license from official registry metadata (permissive MIT/Apache-2.0/BSD may be accepted; free download does not imply an acceptable license). | Dependency additions and updates | none stated
